WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.143
&gt;&gt; The role of CFO

00:00:01.143 --> 00:00:03.437
has changed dramatically.

00:00:03.437 --> 00:00:05.779
CFOs were supposed to be experts in

00:00:05.779 --> 00:00:07.557
accounting and finance,

00:00:07.557 --> 00:00:09.672
now in dynamic environments.

00:00:09.672 --> 00:00:14.078
They are expected to be experts

00:00:14.078 --> 00:00:17.472
in strategy, as well.

00:00:17.472 --> 00:00:18.274
[MUSIC]

00:00:18.274 --> 00:00:20.115
&gt;&gt; I need it a course that will

00:00:20.115 --> 00:00:22.301
help me to become a better CFO.

00:00:22.301 --> 00:00:23.742
&gt;&gt; The ability to become more

00:00:23.742 --> 00:00:25.643
engaged in financial matters with

00:00:25.643 --> 00:00:27.542
our company was an opportunity for

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:28.400
advancement.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.313
&gt;&gt; We expose the participants

00:00:30.313 --> 00:00:32.808
to experts at the Stanford Graduate

00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:35.054
School of Business who have done

00:00:35.054 --> 00:00:37.632
research in the area of leadership,

00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:39.890
as well as strategic thinking.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.295
The participants,

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:43.607
by engaging with these experts as

00:00:43.607 --> 00:00:46.167
well as amongst themselves, will be

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:48.728
able to learn these attributes and,

00:00:48.728 --> 00:00:50.793
in a way that helps accelerate

00:00:50.793 --> 00:00:52.876
their path becoming the CFO.

00:00:52.876 --> 00:00:54.977
&gt;&gt; I've moved from the technical

00:00:54.977 --> 00:00:56.754
aspects of being a finance

00:00:56.754 --> 00:00:59.260
professional to a strategic partner

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.632
and I was looking for

00:01:00.632 --> 00:01:02.650
a class that would help me jump

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:03.970
to the next level.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:05.754
&gt;&gt; We want the participants to gain

00:01:05.754 --> 00:01:07.738
a greater understanding of current

00:01:07.738 --> 00:01:09.731
trends in finance and technology.

00:01:09.731 --> 00:01:11.770
Develop a long-term vision and

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.037
appreciate strategy frameworks,

00:01:14.037 --> 00:01:16.227
assess and enhance their personal

00:01:16.227 --> 00:01:18.116
leadership style to be change

00:01:18.116 --> 00:01:20.231
agents that drive innovation and

00:01:20.231 --> 00:01:22.270
lead to cultural change in their

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.418
organizations.

00:01:23.418 --> 00:01:24.667
&gt;&gt; Here at Stanford,

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.773
they give you the best of the best

00:01:26.773 --> 00:01:28.256
of what is happening in

00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:30.533
the world of finance in strategy.

00:01:30.533 --> 00:01:31.328
&gt;&gt; I'm going to take back

00:01:31.328 --> 00:01:32.264
a different attitude,

00:01:32.264 --> 00:01:33.348
a different perspective.

00:01:33.348 --> 00:01:36.319
&gt;&gt; It's not only the professor's,

00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:38.982
the lectures, the cases, but

00:01:38.982 --> 00:01:41.552
also the whole environment.

00:01:41.552 --> 00:01:43.143
&gt;&gt; The ECFO program has been

00:01:43.143 --> 00:01:45.270
a fantastic opportunity for me.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.140
&gt;&gt; This program is supporting me in

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.159
every way not only me,

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:53.254
it will support my organization.

00:01:53.254 --> 00:01:56.512
&gt;&gt; It has been a transformational

00:01:56.512 --> 00:01:58.020
experience.

